[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Sunnypilot/Openpilot Operational Requirements
VERSION: 0.1
STATUS: DRAFT

[METADATA]
NAME: GeneratedOn
VALUE: 2025-10-30

[METADATA]
NAME: SourceRepository
VALUE: mr.one_sunnypilot

[SECTION]
TITLE: Taxonomy

[TEXT]
This document classifies each requirement with tags in the form domain.* to satisfy the requested taxa covering the operational subsystems of sunnypilot/openpilot. The domains used are:
- domain.system
- domain.power
- domain.sensing
- domain.localization
- domain.planning
- domain.controls
- domain.vehicle
- domain.safety
- domain.driver
- domain.ui
- domain.data
- domain.connectivity
- domain.software
- domain.sunnypilot

[SECTION]
TITLE: System Architecture

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-001
TITLE: Managed Process Lifecycle
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The platform shall start, monitor, and stop runtime services according to the conditional predicates defined in the managed process registry so that only hardware-appropriate daemons run for each vehicle state.
RATIONALE: Implemented by the managed process table in system/manager/process_config.py which wires guard functions, Params, and CarParams into PythonProcess, NativeProcess, and DaemonProcess definitions.
TAGS: [domain.system]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-002
TITLE: Persistent Parameter Store
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The platform shall provide a persistent key-value store accessible across processes for configuration, toggles, and state exchange.
RATIONALE: common/params.py defines the Params interface with shared memory and filesystem backends consumed throughout the codebase including controls and sunnylink utilities.
TAGS: [domain.system]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-003
TITLE: Messaging Fabric
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The system shall use a publish-subscribe messaging fabric to exchange cap'n proto structured messages between all runtime processes.
RATIONALE: cereal/messaging and the generated service definitions underpin SubMaster and PubMaster usage across modules such as selfdrive/controls/controlsd.py and system/sensord/sensord.py.
TAGS: [domain.system]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-004
TITLE: Real-Time Scheduling
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The runtime shall configure thread affinity and priority for time-critical loops to meet deterministic timing guarantees.
RATIONALE: common/realtime.py exposes config_realtime_process used by controlsd, locationd, dmonitoringd, and other services to request specific cores and priorities.
TAGS: [domain.system]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-005
TITLE: Hardware Abstraction
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The platform shall detect device type and expose hardware-specific paths and capabilities to dependent services.
RATIONALE: system/hardware modules and hw.Paths provide environment detection leveraged in process_config, modeld initialization, and sunnylink utilities.
TAGS: [domain.system]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-006
TITLE: Boot Orchestration
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The launch sequence shall bootstrap platform-specific launchers and fall back to the generic entrypoint when specialized launchers are unavailable.
RATIONALE: launch_openpilot.sh dispatches to device-specific launch_chffrplus.sh while ensuring a fallback path for non-C3 hardware.
TAGS: [domain.system]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-007
TITLE: Lifecycle Parameter Clearance
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: Manager initialization shall clear parameter namespaces flagged for lifecycle transitions before any runtime services start to prevent stale state from affecting process predicates.
RATIONALE: system/manager/manager.py clears ParamKeyFlag scoped keys for manager start, onroad, offroad, and ignition events prior to preloading managed processes.
TAGS: [domain.system]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-008
TITLE: Device Registration and Logging Context
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The runtime shall complete device registration and bind logging metadata including git identity, dongle id, and hardware serial before launching managed processes.
RATIONALE: manager_init in system/manager/manager.py registers the device, sets environment variables, and configures sentry/cloudlog context ahead of process preparation.
TAGS: [domain.system]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-009
TITLE: Process Health Broadcasting
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The process manager shall continuously publish aggregated process state snapshots so downstream modules can react to missing or unhealthy daemons.
RATIONALE: system/manager/manager.py composes managerState messages from managed_processes and publishes them over cereal messaging each loop iteration.
TAGS: [domain.system]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Power and Thermal Management

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PWR-001
TITLE: Offroad Power Budget Enforcement
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The device shall integrate offroad power usage and request shutdown when voltage, capacity, or offroad duration thresholds are exceeded to protect the vehicle battery.
RATIONALE: system/hardware/power_monitoring.py computes battery capacity and triggers should_shutdown, which hardwared uses to set DoShutdown when thresholds are met.
TAGS: [domain.power]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PWR-002
TITLE: Thermal and Startup Gating
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The hardware daemon shall only assert the started state when ignition, startup prerequisites, and thermal bands satisfy configured criteria, otherwise it keeps the device in power-save.
RATIONALE: system/hardware/hardwared.py evaluates ignition, startup_conditions, and thermal_status before toggling HARDWARE.set_power_save and publishing deviceState.started.
TAGS: [domain.power]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PWR-003
TITLE: Active Cooling Control
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The platform shall command cooling fans with platform-specific controllers based on filtered component temperatures.
RATIONALE: hardware_thread in system/hardware/hardwared.py instantiates TiciFanController and calls update to compute fanSpeedPercentDesired from temperature bands.
TAGS: [domain.power]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PWR-004
TITLE: Device Telemetry Emission
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The hardware daemon shall publish CPU, GPU, network, and fan telemetry along with statsd gauges for runtime diagnostics.
RATIONALE: system/hardware/hardwared.py populates deviceState metrics and samples statlog gauges for CPU usage, temperatures, power draw, and network state each cycle.
TAGS: [domain.power]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Sensing and Perception

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEN-001
TITLE: Camera Frame Acquisition
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The vision subsystem shall capture road-facing camera frames and publish them via shared memory for downstream neural inference.
RATIONALE: selfdrive/modeld/modeld.py consumes VisionIpcClient streams produced by system/camerad to feed model runners.
TAGS: [domain.sensing]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEN-002
TITLE: IMU and Sensor Collection
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The system shall collect accelerometer, gyroscope, temperature, and magnetometer data using dedicated sensor drivers with interrupt and polling loops.
RATIONALE: system/sensord/sensord.py manages LSM6DS3 and MMC5603 sensors, publishes via messaging, and enforces data validity checks.
TAGS: [domain.sensing]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEN-003
TITLE: Radar Lead Processing
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The perception stack shall process radar tracks into lead vehicle estimates for planning and driver assistance features.
RATIONALE: selfdrive/controls/radard aggregates radarState data and the sunnypilot ControlsExt exposes leadOne and leadTwo fields through custom.CarControlSP messages.
TAGS: [domain.sensing]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEN-004
TITLE: Model Input Preparation
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The perception subsystem shall preprocess camera and contextual inputs into tensors compatible with the active driving model architecture.
RATIONALE: selfdrive/modeld/modeld.py manages InputQueues, OpenCL transformations, and numpy buffers that align with metadata-defined input shapes.
TAGS: [domain.sensing]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEN-005
TITLE: Calibration Data Ingestion
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The system shall ingest live calibration measurements and feed them to components needing device pose alignment.
RATIONALE: selfdrive/locationd/locationd.py handles liveCalibration updates and controlsd reads pose via PoseCalibrator for curvature estimation.
TAGS: [domain.sensing]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEN-006
TITLE: Sensor Health Monitoring
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The sensing pipeline shall reject non-finite, time-skewed, or out-of-range sensor readings to maintain estimator stability.
RATIONALE: LocationEstimator in selfdrive/locationd/locationd.py applies sanity thresholds, timestamp validation, and resets for invalid accelerometer, gyro, and camera odometry data.
TAGS: [domain.sensing]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Localization and Mapping

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LOC-001
TITLE: Pose Estimation Filter
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The system shall maintain a fused vehicle pose estimate using a Kalman filter across IMU, camera odometry, and calibration sources.
RATIONALE: PoseKalman integration within locationd aggregates ObservationKind inputs to track position, orientation, and velocity with error checking.
TAGS: [domain.localization]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LOC-002
TITLE: Calibration Maintenance
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The localization stack shall continuously update device-to-vehicle calibration and expose it to downstream consumers.
RATIONALE: locationd updates device_from_calib matrices and publishes pose and calibration outputs consumed by controlsd and selfdrived.
TAGS: [domain.localization]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LOC-003
TITLE: Latency Compensation Parameters
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The localization services shall publish latency estimates used to compensate control loops for actuation lag.
RATIONALE: sunnypilot.sunnypilot.livedelay.helpers provides lateral delay parameters retrieved by controlsd and applied to torque controllers.
TAGS: [domain.localization]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LOC-004
TITLE: Map Data Lifecycle
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The system shall manage OpenStreetMap extracts by installing updates, cleaning stale data, and scheduling refresh operations.
RATIONALE: sunnypilot/mapd/mapd_manager.py orchestrates versioned downloads, cleanup, and Ratekeeper-driven refresh loops writing Params alerts.
TAGS: [domain.localization]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LOC-005
TITLE: GPS Backend Selection
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The platform shall switch between ublox and Qualcomm GPS backends based on hardware availability while reflecting status in Params.
RATIONALE: process_config predicates ublox, qcomgps, and UbloxAvailable flags ensuring the correct GPS daemon is launched per detected hardware.
TAGS: [domain.localization]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Planning and Prediction

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PLA-001
TITLE: Model-Based Trajectory Planning
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The planning subsystem shall consume neural network predictions to generate desired curvature and acceleration trajectories for the vehicle.
RATIONALE: selfdrive/modeld/modeld.py parses model outputs into ModelDataV2.Action which plannerd and controlsd use for actuation.
TAGS: [domain.planning]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PLA-002
TITLE: Longitudinal Plan Synthesis
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The planner shall synthesize longitudinal targets considering model outputs, lead vehicles, and stopping conditions.
RATIONALE: selfdrive/controls/plannerd integrates lead data from radard and modeld actions to publish longitudinalPlan messages consumed by controlsd.
TAGS: [domain.planning]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PLA-003
TITLE: Onroad Event Integration
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The planner shall incorporate onroad events to adjust or inhibit control actions when safety overrides are active.
RATIONALE: controlsd evaluates onroadEvents override flags before enabling longitudinal control, demonstrating event-aware planning integration.
TAGS: [domain.planning]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PLA-004
TITLE: Personality and HUD Feedback
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The planning outputs shall include driver personality and lead visibility hints for display on the HUD.
RATIONALE: controlsd.publish populates hudControl fields such as leadDistanceBars and leadVisible derived from selfdriveState and longitudinalPlan.
TAGS: [domain.planning]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PLA-005
TITLE: Lane Change Meta Handling
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The planning stack shall interpret model-provided lane change metadata to control blinkers and lateral behavior.
RATIONALE: controlsd.state_control sets blinker commands when modelV2.meta.laneChangeState indicates a lane change in progress.
TAGS: [domain.planning]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Controls and Actuation

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CTRL-001
TITLE: Longitudinal Control Loop
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The control subsystem shall compute throttle and brake actuator commands using PID control bounded by vehicle-specific limits.
RATIONALE: controlsd invokes LongControl.update with PID accel limits from the car interface to fill CarControl.actuators.accel.
TAGS: [domain.controls]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CTRL-002
TITLE: Lateral Control Selection
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The controller shall select the appropriate lateral controller implementation based on CarParams steer control type and tuning mode.
RATIONALE: controlsd constructor instantiates LatControlAngle, LatControlPID, or LatControlTorque according to steerControlType and lateralTuning.
TAGS: [domain.controls]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CTRL-003
TITLE: Safety-Limited Actuation
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The control loop shall detect safety-limited steering output and adjust subsequent requests to respect actuator feedback.
RATIONALE: controlsd.publish compares commanded torque or steering angle against carOutput to set steer_limited_by_safety flags.
TAGS: [domain.controls]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CTRL-004
TITLE: Finite Actuator Validation
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The controller shall ensure actuator commands are finite numeric values before publishing to the vehicle bus.
RATIONALE: controlsd iterates through ACTUATOR_FIELDS and resets non-finite values while logging errors to cloudlog.
TAGS: [domain.controls]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CTRL-005
TITLE: Latency Compensation
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The control subsystem shall compensate for measured lateral delay when computing torque controller limits.
RATIONALE: controlsd retrieves lateralDelay via get_lat_delay and updates LatControlTorque extension lag parameters accordingly.
TAGS: [domain.controls]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CTRL-006
TITLE: Pose-Aware Actuation
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The controller shall incorporate calibrated orientation and angular velocity when available to improve downstream control consumers.
RATIONALE: controlsd.publish populates CarControl orientationNED and angularVelocity fields when calibrated pose data exists.
TAGS: [domain.controls]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CTRL-007
TITLE: Online Vehicle Parameter Learning
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The control stack shall maintain live estimates of steer ratio, stiffness, and angle offsets while bounding their validity for use in control loops.
RATIONALE: selfdrive/locationd/paramsd.py runs VehicleParamsLearner to fuse livePose, carState, and calibration inputs, clipping outputs and publishing liveParameters with validity checks.
TAGS: [domain.controls]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Vehicle Interface and Safety

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VEH-001
TITLE: Vehicle Fingerprint Selection
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The system shall select vehicle-specific interfaces based on the detected car fingerprint.
RATIONALE: controlsd instantiates the correct CarInterface via opendbc.car.car_helpers.interfaces keyed on CP.carFingerprint.
TAGS: [domain.vehicle]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VEH-002
TITLE: Safety Model Enforcement
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The platform shall enforce panda safety model policies before actuating CAN messages.
RATIONALE: panda firmware and python bindings in panda/ ensure safety model selection and message gating aligned with CarParams.SafetyModel.
TAGS: [domain.vehicle]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VEH-003
TITLE: Fault-Driven Control Disablement
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The control subsystem shall disengage or inhibit actuation when vehicle-reported faults or overrides are active.
RATIONALE: controlsd.state_control checks steerFault flags, standstill status, and overrideLongitudinal events before enabling latActive or longActive.
TAGS: [domain.vehicle]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VEH-004
TITLE: Cruise Control Mediation
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The vehicle interface shall manage cruise control overrides, cancellations, and resumes based on planner state and vehicle feedback.
RATIONALE: controlsd.publish sets cruiseControl override, cancel, and resume flags depending on openpilotLongitudinalControl, shouldStop, and carState.
TAGS: [domain.vehicle]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VEH-005
TITLE: Car Output Feedback Integration
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The controller shall incorporate car controller actuator feedback to adjust engagement state.
RATIONALE: CarOutput comparison in controlsd.publish determines steer safety limitation and informs future actuator saturation handling.
TAGS: [domain.vehicle]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VEH-006
TITLE: Unified Engagement Safeguards
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The selfdrived layer shall clear or replace engagement events when vehicle conditions prohibit activation.
RATIONALE: sunnypilot/mads/mads.py manipulates events such as wrongGear and pedalPressed to ensure safe engagement states for ModularAssistiveDrivingSystem.
TAGS: [domain.vehicle]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VEH-007
TITLE: Panda Firmware Stewardship
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The platform shall verify and flash panda firmware, recover DFU devices, and reset internal pandas before starting CAN bridge execution.
RATIONALE: selfdrive/pandad/pandad.py enumerates pandas, flashes mismatched firmware signatures, recovers DFU units, and restarts pandad with the discovered serial order.
TAGS: [domain.vehicle]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VEH-008
TITLE: Car Parameter Persistence and SecOC Provisioning
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The car interface shall cache CarParams and CarParamsSP to persistent storage and provision SecOC keys prior to enabling actuator control.
RATIONALE: selfdrive/car/card.py stores CarParams variants in Params, migrates SecOC keys, and sets safetyConfigs before signaling ControlsReady.
TAGS: [domain.vehicle]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VEH-009
TITLE: CAN Bridging and Cruise Mediation Loop
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The car interface shall translate CAN traffic into carState, carOutput, and carParams messages while publishing actuator commands at the Ratekeeper-controlled 100Hz cycle.
RATIONALE: selfdrive/car/card.py uses can_capnp_to_list to update CarInterface, publishes carState/carOutput, and sends actuator CAN via Ratekeeper alongside VCruiseHelper updates.
TAGS: [domain.vehicle]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Operational Safety Governance

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SAFE-001
TITLE: Engagement Event Evaluation
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The supervisory logic shall synthesize events from car state, planner, driver monitoring, and model metadata to determine engagement eligibility and surface onroad events.
RATIONALE: selfdrive/selfdrived/selfdrived.py aggregates Events and EventsSP in update_events, combining onroadEvents, car-specific events, and planner metadata before updating the state machine.
TAGS: [domain.safety]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SAFE-002
TITLE: Device Health Alerting
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The supervisory layer shall raise alerts for thermal, storage, memory, and fan malfunctions using telemetry from deviceState and peripheralState.
RATIONALE: update_events in selfdrive/selfdrived/selfdrived.py adds overheat, outOfSpace, lowMemory, and fanMalfunction events when device metrics exceed thresholds.
TAGS: [domain.safety]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SAFE-003
TITLE: Process and Messaging Watchdog
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The supervisory logic shall monitor managerState, socket liveness, and frequency metrics and emit processNotRunning or commIssue events when checks fail.
RATIONALE: selfdrive/selfdrived/selfdrived.py inspects managerState process statuses and SubMaster health to log process_not_running and add commIssue or camera alerts.
TAGS: [domain.safety]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SAFE-004
TITLE: Safety Model Alignment
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The supervisory layer shall compare panda safety models and controlsAllowed flags against CarParams expectations and trigger controlsMismatch on persistent mismatches.
RATIONALE: selfdrive/selfdrived/selfdrived.py evaluates pandaStates against CP.safetyConfigs and increments mismatch counters to raise controlsMismatch or cruiseMismatch events.
TAGS: [domain.safety]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Driver Interaction and Monitoring

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DM-001
TITLE: Driver Monitoring Loop
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The system shall evaluate driver attention metrics and publish driverMonitoringState at 20Hz when the monitoring model provides updates.
RATIONALE: selfdrive/monitoring/dmonitoringd.py runs DriverMonitoring.run_step when driverStateV2 updates and publishes the resulting state via messaging.
TAGS: [domain.driver]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DM-002
TITLE: Always-On Monitoring Toggle
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: Driver monitoring shall support runtime toggles for always-on behavior fetched from persistent parameters.
RATIONALE: dmonitoringd reloads AlwaysOnDM from Params every 40 frames and updates the DriverMonitoring instance.
TAGS: [domain.driver]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DM-003
TITLE: RHD Detection Persistence
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The monitoring subsystem shall persist detected right-hand-drive configuration when sufficient wheel position evidence accumulates.
RATIONALE: dmonitoringd stores IsRhdDetected via params.put_bool_nonblocking when wheel positions exceed thresholds.
TAGS: [domain.driver]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DM-004
TITLE: Engagement Event Mediation
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: Driver assist extensions shall mediate engagement and disengagement events based on pedal usage, cruise availability, and manual inputs.
RATIONALE: sunnypilot/mads/mads.py inspects button events, pedal presses, and cruise state to add or clear custom OnroadEventSP alerts.
TAGS: [domain.driver]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DM-005
TITLE: Silent Alert Management
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The driver assistance logic shall downgrade certain alerts to silent variants when assistive steering remains available in paused modes.
RATIONALE: MADS replace_event and transition_paused_state functions map core alerts to silentLkasDisable or silentSeatbeltNotLatched conditions.
TAGS: [domain.driver]

[SECTION]
TITLE: User Interface and Alerts

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: UI-001
TITLE: UI Process Availability
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: A dedicated UI process shall run continuously to render onroad and offroad displays with watchdog supervision.
RATIONALE: process_config launches selfdrive/ui with watchdog_max_dt guards ensuring UI responsiveness on embedded hardware.
TAGS: [domain.ui]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: UI-002
TITLE: Sound Alert Generation
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The system shall generate auditory alerts based on onroad events and planner state transitions.
RATIONALE: process_config schedules soundd which listens to events and plays audio feedback during control transitions.
TAGS: [domain.ui]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: UI-003
TITLE: HUD Feedback Population
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The controller shall populate HUD control fields with speed, lane, and lead information for visual display.
RATIONALE: controlsd.publish fills hudControl setSpeed, lanesVisible, and lead indicators prior to messaging.
TAGS: [domain.ui]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: UI-004
TITLE: Offroad Alerting
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The system shall raise offroad alerts when maintenance actions, such as map downloads, are required.
RATIONALE: sunnypilot/mapd/mapd_manager.set_offroad_alert posts Offroad_OSMUpdateRequired based on cleanup state and Params flags.
TAGS: [domain.ui]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Data Logging and Diagnostics

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DATA-001
TITLE: Route Logging
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The platform shall record onroad data segments for later analysis and replay.
RATIONALE: process_config schedules loggerd and encoderd to capture logs whenever the vehicle is onroad.
TAGS: [domain.data]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DATA-002
TITLE: Telemetry Publishing
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The system shall publish diagnostic messages for process health and system metrics.
RATIONALE: system/logmessaged and system/statsd processes stream log messages and statistics as configured in process_config.
TAGS: [domain.data]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DATA-003
TITLE: Cloud Logging Upload
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: Recorded logs shall be uploaded when uploader prerequisites are satisfied and upload toggles permit it.
RATIONALE: process_config includes uploader with uploader_ready predicate honoring OnroadUploads and NetworkMetered Params.
TAGS: [domain.data]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DATA-004
TITLE: Tombstone Crash Capture
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The system shall capture crash tombstones on embedded hardware when supported.
RATIONALE: process_config launches tombstoned on devices that are not PCs to capture native crash dumps.
TAGS: [domain.data]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DATA-005
TITLE: Offroad Backup Management
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The system shall manage device backups during offroad periods when sunnylink connectivity is ready.
RATIONALE: process_config adds sunnypilot.sunnylink.backups.manager guarded by sunnylink_ready_shim and only_offroad predicates.
TAGS: [domain.data]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DATA-006
TITLE: Status Packet Logging
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The platform shall periodically log aggregated hardware status packets and persist the last offroad snapshot for diagnostics.
RATIONALE: system/hardware/hardwared.py emits cloudlog STATUS_PACKET events every ten minutes and stores the last offroad packet in the LastOffroadStatusPacket param.
TAGS: [domain.data]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Connectivity and Cloud Services

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NET-001
TITLE: Athena Connectivity Daemon
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The platform shall run a persistent Athena daemon manager to maintain cloud connectivity and telemetry sessions.
RATIONALE: system/athena/manage_athenad.py supervises the athenad process, binding device metadata and restarting on exit.
TAGS: [domain.connectivity]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NET-002
TITLE: Sunnylink Registration Management
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The system shall manage sunnylink registration state and trigger registration flows when enabled but unregistered.
RATIONALE: process_config launches sunnylink_registration_manager using sunnylink_need_register_shim defined in sunnypilot/sunnylink/utils.py.
TAGS: [domain.connectivity]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NET-003
TITLE: Sunnylink Uploader Eligibility
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: Cloud uploads via sunnylink shall respect network metering and registration status before starting transfers.
RATIONALE: sunnypilot/sunnylink/utils.py exposes use_sunnylink_uploader which checks Params before uploader processes run.
TAGS: [domain.connectivity]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NET-004
TITLE: Remote API Token Handling
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The platform shall support retrieval and storage of sunnylink API tokens for authenticated service access.
RATIONALE: sunnypilot/sunnylink/utils.py implements get_api_token and parameter persistence using SunnylinkApi.
TAGS: [domain.connectivity]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NET-005
TITLE: WebRTC Teleoperation Bridge
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The platform shall bridge configured messaging services, video, and audio over WebRTC sessions to support remote monitoring and teleoperation tooling.
RATIONALE: system/webrtc/webrtcd.py orchestrates StreamSession objects that map cereal publishers/subscribers onto RTC data channels alongside LiveStream video and audio tracks.
TAGS: [domain.connectivity]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Software Management and Tooling

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SW-001
TITLE: Model Bundle Management
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The system shall download, verify, and activate driving model bundles based on user selection and availability.
RATIONALE: sunnypilot/models/manager.py orchestrates ModelFetcher downloads, SHA verification, and active bundle persistence via Params.
TAGS: [domain.software]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SW-002
TITLE: Model Runner Selection
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The runtime shall launch the appropriate model runner binary (stock, SNPE, or tinygrad) according to active runner choice.
RATIONALE: process_config guards modeld, modeld_snpe, and modeld_tinygrad with get_active_model_runner predicates from sunnypilot.models.helpers.
TAGS: [domain.software]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SW-003
TITLE: Software Update Scheduling
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The system shall defer updater execution to offroad periods on embedded hardware.
RATIONALE: process_config schedules updated with only_offroad predicate and disabled on PC targets.
TAGS: [domain.software]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SW-004
TITLE: Developer Tooling Support
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: The platform shall offer optional tooling processes such as copyparty or github runner when corresponding binaries exist and toggles are enabled.
RATIONALE: process_config conditionally appends copyparty-sfx and github_runner_start based on filesystem checks and Params flags.
TAGS: [domain.software]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Sunnypilot Extensions

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SP-001
TITLE: Controls Extension Messaging
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: Sunnypilot shall extend control messaging with custom CarControlSP payloads carrying radar and MADS state.
RATIONALE: sunnypilot/selfdrive/controls/controlsd_ext.py packages radarState leads and selfdriveStateSP fields into carControlSP messages.
TAGS: [domain.sunnypilot]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SP-002
TITLE: Blinker Pause Lateral Handling
STATUS: accepted
STATEMENT: Sunnypilot shall pause lateral control when blinker-based pause logic determines manual intervention is desired.
RATIONALE: ControlsExt.get_lat_active consults BlinkerPauseLateral which reads Params to temporarily disable latActive.
TAGS: [domain.sunnypilot]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SP-003
TITLE: Modular Assistive Driving System State Machine
STATUS: accepted
